  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Stop the turn – one v one",
  "description": "An area of about 30 × 40 metres with a full-size goal and goalkeeper. The passers stand in a short line at the far end and the defenders in a short line by a cone at the side. Attacker B stands with their back to goal and defender X behind, on the goal side.\n\nA plays the ball in to B, who tries to turn and score. X must stop the turn and win the ball at the right moment, with no help from anyone. If X wins the ball, X scores a point by passing it back to A.\n\nRotation after each attempt: A becomes the attacker, B joins the defenders' line and X joins the passers. Competition: every player counts their goals and the balls they win. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stay close – an arm's length behind – so the attacker feels you, but not so close they can spin round you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stand slightly to one side and shut the turn that way."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Watch the ball, not the body feints."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Go in for the ball when the touch is too heavy or the attacker looks down."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
